---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import {dropped,statusCounts,toHref} from '../lib';
---
<Layout title="Dropped and redraft entries | PsychTerms"><div class="article-wrap prose"><p class="breadcrumb"><a href={toHref()}>psychterms.org</a> / Dropped</p><h1>Dropped entries</h1><p>These failed entries are excluded from term pages, search and definition downloads. The forward-only rule applies to each entry, not its headword.</p><p><strong>Dropped ({statusCounts.dropped}):</strong> headwords treated as out of scope, pending a scope read. They are not redrafted.</p><p><strong>Redraft ({statusCounts.redraft}):</strong> in-scope headwords whose definitions failed their source packets. These headwords return to the candidate pool marked “new packet required”. Each replacement is a new entry with new provenance and its own two independent reads.</p>{dropped.length ? <ul>{dropped.map((entry:any)=><li data-entry-content data-entry-id={entry.id} data-entry-status={entry.status}><span class="tag review-status">{entry.status==='redraft' ? 'Redraft' : 'Dropped'}</span> <strong>{entry.term}</strong>: {entry.reason}<p class="small">{entry.status==='redraft' ? 'New packet required.' : 'Scope read pending.'}</p>{entry.latest_sourcing && <p class="small">Latest sourcing: {entry.latest_sourcing.reason}.</p>}<p class="small">{entry.sources.map((source:any)=><span><a href={source.url}>{source.citation}</a> · <a href={source.licence_url}>{source.licence}</a> </span>)}</p></li>)}</ul> : <p>No failed entries.</p>}<p><a href={toHref('downloads/redraft-candidates.json')}>Headwords requiring new packets (JSON)</a> · <a href={toHref('downloads/release-note.md')}>Status counts and release note</a></p></div></Layout>
